# End-to-end EMULATOR test for the Duet3 Mini 5+ (Microchip SAME54P20,
# run on the pin-/register-compatible samd51p20 build) in DETERMINISTIC
# TICK MODE. Boots klipper firmware under Renode against the duet3-mini
# pin map, completes klippy identify + clocksync, brings up the full MCU
# config (4 TMC2209s on multi-drop UART, 2 software-PWM heaters, a
# heater_fan, endstops, adc_scaled thermistors), reads the thermistors
# through the SAMX5 ADC, round-trips the four TMC2209 register files over
# their shared software UART, and exercises interactive gcode.
#
# This is the SAMD51/SAME54 per-printer test, the counterpart to
# samd51_smoke (boot only). What it adds over the smoke test:
#
#   - TMC2209 MULTI-DROP UART. All four drivers share uart_pin PA1 /
#     tx_pin PA0 / select_pins PD0 with uart_address 0..3, reusing the
#     renode_hooks sw_uart responder. _drive_rx drives the firmware-side
#     RX bit through the SAMD51 PORT model (gpio_a.OnGPIO) - the
#     samd51p20.repl now declares gpio_a..gpio_d (GPIOPort.SAMD21_GPIO,
#     which serves the layout-identical SAMX5 PortGroup registers). A
#     single shared sw_uart state + register file serves all four
#     addresses because klippy initialises drivers sequentially - the
#     same multidrop path skr_pico / skr_mini_e3_v3 exercise. DUMP_TMC
#     below reads the live register file for stepper_x and the extruder;
#     the IOIN read returning version=0x21 proves the multidrop UART read
#     path round-tripped.
#
#   - adc_scaled thermistors through the new test/emulator/
#     samd51_adc_stub.py. The SAMX5 ADC register layout differs from
#     SAMD21's (INPUTCTRL@0x04, SWTRIG@0x14, INTFLAG@0x2E, SYNCBUSY@0x30,
#     RESULT@0x40), so it needs its own stub; the stub also returns
#     SYNCBUSY=0 so adc_init's busy-waits fall through. All four channels
#     land on ADC1 (vref=7, vssa=6, extruder PC1=11, bed PC0=10). vref
#     and vssa carry distinct values so adc_scaled's (vref - vssa)
#     divisor is non-zero (a zero divisor raises ZeroDivisionError in
#     extras/adc_scaled.py); both sensors read ~36 C.
#
# The real Duet3 Mini host link is USB-CDC; the firmware here is the
# generic serial-mode samd51p20 build (host link on PA10/PA11) and the
# test exercises the pin map, which is independent of the host link. The
# gated path is motion-free.
DICTIONARY samd51p20.dict
CONFIG duet3_mini.cfg
EMULATOR duet3_mini.fixture.json
REQUIRES_EMULATOR  # deterministic-time lockstep needs the real backend

# Interactive gcode round-trip against real firmware in tick mode.
M114
M105
# Read back the live TMC register file over the multi-drop UART for the
# first and last drivers (uart_address 0 and 3).
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=stepper_x
DUMP_TMC STEPPER=extruder

# klippy connected, loaded the dictionary, and built the full config
# against real firmware.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Configured MCU 'mcu'"
# DUMP_TMC dumped the first and last drivers; the IOIN read returning the
# TMC version byte (0x21) proves the multi-drop UART read path returned
# framed, CRC-valid responses for both addresses.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC stepper_x"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "DUMP_TMC extruder"
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "version=0x21"
# Positive proof the SAMX5 ADC delivered samples through adc_scaled: both
# thermistors read ~36 C, so a periodic Stats line carries "temp=3x". A
# broken ADC leaves them at temp=0.0 with no shutdown.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "temp=3"
# adc_scaled requires (vref - vssa) != 0; without distinct vref/vssa
# values klippy raises ZeroDivisionError in adc_scaled.handle_callback.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ZeroDivisionError"
# A broken UART round-trip surfaces as a TMC init failure or a read error.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to read tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to write tmc uart"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
# A renode-side crash (wrong sysbus peripheral, hook callback error)
# kills serial; klippy then gets EOF and identify / TMC init time out.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Got EOF when reading from device"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "failed to init: Timeout"
# With the deterministic clock the config / TMC / ADC path pushes no
# deadline into the firmware's past, so nothing shuts down.
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "ADC out of range"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Timer too close"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Rescheduled timer in the past"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
